--- !u!1 &1347035039
GameObject:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  serializedVersion: 6
  m_Component:
  - component: {fileID: 1347035041}
  - component: {fileID: 1347035040}
  m_Layer: 0
  m_Name: DemoSequencer
  m_TagString: Untagged
  m_Icon: {fileID: 0}
  m_NavMeshLayer: 0
  m_StaticEditorFlags: 0
  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &1347035040
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1347035039}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: fd2cf5d4ed57e47e29f8c0e4c101cf4a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DemoSequencer
  steps:
  - title: One sine wave
    hint: 'Fourier: any sound can be built from sine waves. This is the building
      block of everything that follows.'
    root: {fileID: 1230930462}
    showExtraControls: 0
  - title: Digital audio is numbers
    hint: About 48,000 numbers a second. Fewer steps per number (bit depth) or fewer
      numbers (holding each one) and the smooth wave becomes a staircase. Listen
      to it get buzzy.
    root: {fileID: 1617734462}
    showExtraControls: 1
  - title: Noise, and shaping it
    hint: 'Noise is every frequency at once. A filter keeps some: low-pass = rumble,
      high-pass = air.'
    root: {fileID: 745179742}
    showExtraControls: 0
  - title: 'Frozen: a rain recording on loop'
    hint: 'A recording is frozen in time. Listen for the seam: it repeats exactly.'
    root: {fileID: 423670050}
    showExtraControls: 0
  - title: 'Thawed: recordings under rules'
    hint: 'The same kind of recordings: a bed loop and 8 single drops. Random choice,
      pitch, volume and timing. One slider: intensity. (Part A: recorded)'
    root: {fileID: 1353655955}
    showExtraControls: 0
  - title: 'Rain, layer 1: droplets'
    hint: 'Slow random noise, raised to the 8th power, lets only its rare peaks through.
      Each peak gates a short sine: a plink.'
    root: {fileID: 1073641091}
    showExtraControls: 0
  - title: 'Rain, layer 2: drips'
    hint: 'A pressure pulse, and sometimes a bubble ringing as it rises: Farnell''s
      physics of a drop.'
    root: {fileID: 820031459}
    showExtraControls: 0
  - title: 'Rain, layers 3 and 4: rumble and ambience'
    hint: Noise around 333 Hz for drops on big surfaces, and a little white noise
      for the distant wash. The full patch.
    root: {fileID: 456807311}
    showExtraControls: 0
  - title: 'One slider: drizzle to storm'
    hint: 'Intensity changes WHAT the sound is, not just how loud: more drops, more
      rumble. A recording cannot do this. (Part B: procedural)'
    root: {fileID: 2037565846}
    showExtraControls: 1
  - title: Your building blocks
    hint: 'Part B gives you two: a Noise Layer (a constant sound) and a Burst Layer
      (short random events). Move the sliders and listen.'
    root: {fileID: 694472354}
    showExtraControls: 0
  - title: 'The reveal: three elements of fire'
    hint: 'Farnell: hissing (gas escaping), crackling (sap bursting), lapping (the
      flames'' roar). Solo each one, then all three, then intensity.'
    root: {fileID: 402391940}
    showExtraControls: 0
  current: 0
  uiScale: 2
